{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["Who was betrothed — designated and set aside for a Hebrew slave: if his master gives him a wife. Similar to it: ״עם חרף נפשו למות״ — he surrendered his life. And so too in the Targum." "Has not been redeemed — for she is not freed and is not like a married woman, to be judged by strangling." "There shall be an inquiry — like ״לא יבקר הכהן״; so Dunash and Menachem explained it. The court investigates whether she was not freed; if not, they do not impose the death penalty upon him as upon one who lies with a married woman."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The scriptural parallel is Judges 5:18; Rashbam does not cite the address.", 2 "Rashbam gives the first part of the explanation (the comparison to לא יבקר) and then the legal consequence in sequence; the logic is: an inquiry (בקרה) establishes her unfreed status, which reduces the penalty."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:06.865236404Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}